{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\n__author__ = 'MoonBall'\n\nimport sys\n# sys.stdin = open('data/D.in', 'r')\nT = 1\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef compute():\n    P, K = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    # Handle special cases\n    if K == 0:\n        print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n        return\n    if K == 1:\n        print(pow(P, P, MOD))\n        return\n\n    # Build adjacency mapping\n    adj = [K * i % P for i in range(P)]\n    \n    # Find cycles using DFS-like traversal\n    visited = [False] * P\n    freq = [0] * P\n    prod = 1\n\n    for node in range(P):\n        if visited[node]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Count cycle length\n        length = 0\n        cur = node\n        while not visited[cur]:\n            visited[cur] = True\n            cur = adj[cur]\n            length += 1\n        \n        if length > 0:\n            freq[length] += 1\n\n    # Apply formula\n    for cycle_len in range(2, P):\n        if freq[cycle_len]:\n            val = cycle_len * freq[cycle_len] + 1\n            prod = (prod * pow(val, freq[cycle_len], MOD)) % MOD\n\n    print(prod)\n\nfor _ in range(T):\n    compute()\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int T = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < T; i++) {\n            compute(sc);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static void compute(Scanner sc) {\n        int P = sc.nextInt();\n        int K = sc.nextInt();\n\n        // Handle special cases\n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n        if (K == 1) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(P, P, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Build adjacency mapping\n        int[] adj = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            adj[i] = (K * i) % P;\n        }\n\n        // Find cycles using DFS-like traversal\n        boolean[] visited = new boolean[P];\n        int[] freq = new int[P];\n        long prod = 1;\n\n        for (int node = 0; node < P; node++) {\n            if (visited[node]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n\n            // Count cycle length\n            int length = 0;\n            int cur = node;\n            while (!visited[cur]) {\n                visited[cur] = true;\n                cur = adj[cur];\n                length++;\n            }\n\n            if (length > 0) {\n                freq[length]++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Apply formula\n        for (int cycle_len = 2; cycle_len < P; cycle_len++) {\n            if (freq[cycle_len] > 0) {\n                long val = (long) cycle_len * freq[cycle_len] + 1;\n                prod = (prod * modPow(val, freq[cycle_len], MOD)) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(prod);\n    }\n\n    static long modPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base = base % mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00011455356434453279, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0002649671514518559, -3.635817120084539e-05, -0.0890028178691864, -0.38769805431365967, -1.07287787614041e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.00022766382608097047, -0.20141616463661194, -0.004079591948539019, -0.4349251985549927, -0.0002109781780745834, -0.014199413359165192, -3.3378546504536644e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -3.099436753473128e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -0.2987501621246338, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.009772317484021187, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -0.0036010199692100286, -0.014165564440190792, -2.50339189733495e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.433168603805825e-05, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.2993727978027891e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -7.986703712958843e-05, -0.11328408867120743, -7.152531907195225e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -6.079655122448457e-06, -5.483612312673358e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.00044050050200894475, -0.011396664194762707, -1.6927575416048057e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00462521705776453, 0.0, -0.00018249277491122484, -0.009759804233908653, -0.07891728729009628, -7.152555099310121e-07, 0.0, -0.6396850943565369, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.933898824470816e-06, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -5.483612312673358e-06, -0.00016425691137555987, -0.00120698066893965, -1.966933996300213e-05, -1.2040065485052764e-05, -3.2186